---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const title = 'About';
const description = 'About Marcelo Ohashi, software architect and author of DevMode.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`${title} | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main-content">
			<h1>{title}</h1>
			<section>
				<h2>About me</h2>
				<p>
					Hey, I'm Marcelo. I'm a software architect who's spent years designing and leading
					teams building microservices, applications, and integration solutions. I've worked
					across a bunch of languages, tools, and methodologies, and I genuinely believe everyone
					on a team can push a product forward, not just the "senior" folks.
				</p>
				<p>
					Lately I've been deep into agentic development, building real things with AI coding
					agents like Kiro and Claude Code instead of just writing code by hand. It's changed how
					I think about software: less about typing every line, more about directing, reviewing,
					and making the right calls at the right moments. This blog is partly a place for me to
					write about what I'm learning there.
				</p>
				<p>
					Outside of work, I tinker with home automation, speak at conferences and workshops when
					I get the chance, and I'm generally the person who can't resist automating something
					that probably didn't need automating.
				</p>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2>About this blog</h2>
				<p>
					This is where I write about cloud native systems, developer tooling, and (more and
					more) what it's actually like to build software alongside AI agents day to day. No
					fluff, no hot takes for the sake of hot takes, just stuff I've actually run into and
					figured out.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

